    "rules": "Classic Sudoku: Every row, column and 3x3 box must contain every number from 1 to 9.\nSkyscrapers: Each digit in the grid represents the height of a building in its cell, and taller buildings obstruct the view of shorter ones behind them: clues outside the grid give the number of buildings visible from that vantage point in the clue's row or column.\nSandwich Sums: A circled clue indicates the sum of the digits between 1 and 9 in the indicated row or column. Circled clues are also Skyscrapers clues.",
